(7683423, 1257519, 45631, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LevT:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> [...] also i think its an extremely fantastic shot with that lens .. did you crop it a lot ... <br/>and answer at your leisure .. :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>only cropped about a half, he was not very far. It is a wonderful lens, the first super-zoom I''ve had that does not disappoint in sharpness or clarity throughout the entire zoom range. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Whilst I have the 40-150 pro f2.8 and the 1.4 teleconverter I find that the images become soft with the 1.4tc and need to be stopped down to f5 to get the sharpness back.  I have been experimenting by shooting both Raw and Jpeg and using the x2 digital zoom for my surf shots.  Generally do this when I am shooting with the lens fully extended to 150mm.  So with the crop factor added and then the 2x digital zoom I get a focal length of 600mm with images that are sharp from f2.8.  Have been pleasantly surprised with the results. If I need more reach I add the 1.4tc.  The image I submitted was one using this method.  I also have the 12-100 lens and I will use this when travelling to get extra reach which makes this lens even more versatile.  The Jpeg files are quite large (approx 8mp).  Anyway, just thought I would mention it in case you haven''t thought to give it a try.  I wont use it for everything but its handy to have<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-01-05 07:51:32.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by LevT: Originally posted by roz: [...] also i think its an extremely fantastic shot with that lens .. did you crop it a lot ... and answer at your leisure .. :)  only cropped about a half, he was not very far. It is a wonderful lens, the first super-zoom I''ve had that does not disappoint in sharpness or clarity throughout the entire zoom range.   Whilst I have the 40-150 pro f2.8 and the 1.4 teleconverter I find that the images become soft with the 1.4tc and need to be stopped down to f5 to get the sharpness back.  I have been experimenting by shooting both Raw and Jpeg and using the x2 digital zoom for my surf shots.  Generally do this when I am shooting with the lens fully extended to 150mm.  So with the crop factor added and then the 2x digital zoom I get a focal length of 600mm with images that are sharp from f2.8.  Have been pleasantly surprised with the results. If I need more reach I add the 1.4tc.  The image I submitted was one using this method.  I also have the 12-100 lens and I will use this when travelling to get extra reach which makes this lens even more versatile.  The Jpeg files are quite large (approx 8mp).  Anyway, just thought I would mention it in case you haven''t thought to give it a try.  I wont use it for everything but its handy to have', '2021-01-05 04:57:53.000000', '2021-01-05 07:51:32.000000', 0),
